      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Drinking nights on quest 3s, the z clashing didn't seem as bad when i was there, but i'll rewatch all the videos later.\n\ni don't believe vrchat can directly solve this issue, hmm, ai is telling me that unity and the quest use single precision floats. but in my observations the pc vrchat has more precision than on quest, so when polygons are close enough they are getting rendered with slightly different positioning based on the exact angle of the camera.\n\ni had to adjust one of my worlds twice, when i switched the unity editor from pc to quest the precision in the editor changed, so i knew to adjust some things. i then uploaded the world and tested on my headset and had to move things a wee bit more.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
